# Copy to .env.local. Values for local development come from `pnpm db:start`.
# The anon key is a public, RLS-constrained key and belongs in the browser bundle.
# There is no service-role key here on purpose: nothing in apps/web may hold one.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Taking card payments. Both optional: with neither set, no card control appears — a business
# that takes only cash is a complete business.
#
# These are **GOLD's own platform credentials** and they stay here permanently. A tenant's
# processor account is never configured through the environment: the business authorizes GOLD
# from their own account and what gets stored is an `acct_` id in a row, which is not a
# credential (constraints.md D27). The money is charged on their account and never reaches a
# balance of ours.
#
# The webhook's signing secret is not here — verifying callbacks is `apps/api`'s.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_CONNECT_CLIENT_ID=

# Turning an address into a point, for weather, travel time and service areas. Optional: with
# this unset there is no lookup and coordinates are typed in by hand, which the locations screen
# says out loud rather than showing two empty boxes (constraints.md D31).
#
# Not a credential. The provider is free and asks in return that every caller identify itself,
# so this is an address somebody can be reached at — an installation that has not said who it is
# has not finished configuring the capability, which is why its absence switches it off.
GEOCODING_CONTACT=

# Drafting a business's setup from a description of it (constraints.md D32). Optional: with this
# unset there is no drafting, and every part of a setup is still configurable by hand on screens
# that predate it — which the setup screen says out loud rather than showing a box that cannot
# work (D31).
#
# A credential, unlike GEOCODING_CONTACT, and GOLD's own rather than a tenant's. Nothing about
# drafting is a business's relationship with a vendor: the platform asks on their behalf and
# hands back a document they own, edit and apply themselves.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Where the tool loop runs (constraints.md D34). Optional: with this unset there is no assistant,
# and the Ask screen says so rather than showing a box that cannot work (D31).
#
# Not a credential. It is the base URL of this repository's own `apps/api` deployment, and the
# only thing sent to it is the question plus the asking person's own access token — which is what
# makes every tool run inside that person's RLS boundary. Which model answers is that
# deployment's decision, including a model on the business's own hardware.
ASSISTANT_API_URL=

# Placing a call (constraints.md D38, D39). All three optional: with any of them unset there is
# no dialling at all, the Call button says why rather than appearing and doing nothing, and
# writing a call down after the fact still works — a business dialling from mobile phones is a
# complete business (D31).
#
# **GOLD's own master account, never a tenant's.** Each business gets a subaccount of it, and
# what is stored against that business is a subaccount identifier — not a credential, which is
# the whole of D39. A tenant pasting a token into a settings form is the shape D27 already
# refused, and it is refused here for the same reason: a secret needs a vault, a rotation story
# and an answer for the day it is revoked, and an identifier needs none of those.
#
# The same account carries text messages from `apps/api`, so these two values exist in both
# deployments on purpose rather than by accident.
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=

# The number a call shows as coming from.
#
# **One per deployment, which is the assumption a floor breaks.** A business needs many numbers,
# chosen by area and assigned to a person or a pool, and that inventory is a table rather than a
# variable. This exists so the first call can be placed before that table does, and it goes away
# when the table arrives.
TELEPHONY_FROM_NUMBER=

# Letting a browser be a telephone, and telling the carrier where to report.
#
# **An API key rather than the account token above**, because the credential a browser holds is
# a short-lived JWT this server signs — naming one person, one application, and expiring in an
# hour. The account token could not do that without being the thing handed out.
#
# The application is what the carrier fetches instructions from when a browser starts a call.
# Point its voice URL at `<TELEPHONY_CALLBACK_URL>/voice/outbound`.
TWILIO_API_KEY_SID=
TWILIO_API_KEY_SECRET=
TWILIO_TWIML_APP_SID=

# The public base of this repository's own `apps/api` deployment, where the carrier reports what
# happened to a call. Passed per call rather than configured once at the carrier, so a preview
# and production can run side by side without one collecting the other's callbacks.
#
# Usually the same deployment as ASSISTANT_API_URL, and a separate variable because the two
# features are separately configurable everywhere else here — one switch must not turn off the
# other.
TELEPHONY_CALLBACK_URL=
